      clinicalImportance: 'ELISA is a cornerstone of immunodiagnostics, used for detecting infectious diseases (HIV, hepatitis), hormone levels (TSH, hCG), tumor markers, autoimmune antibodies, cytokines, and allergen-specific IgE. It offers high sensitivity and specificity for quantitative and qualitative analysis.',
      applications: ['HIV and hepatitis screening', 'Hormone quantification (TSH, hCG, cortisol)', 'Tumor marker detection (PSA, CA-125)', 'Cytokine and chemokine measurement', 'Allergen-specific IgE testing', 'Drug and vaccine potency testing'],
